  "facts": [
    "The Sherman Minton Bridge, opened December 22, 1961, was named after former U.S. Senator and Supreme Court justice Sherman Minton, a native of New Albany, honoring his legacy on the day the lower deck opened.",
    "Built with T1 steel, the bridge’s double‑deck arch was deemed “fracture critical” in the 1960s, a design that required meticulous inspections after cracks discovered in 2011, prompting a $20 million repair.",
    "After a coal‑barge collision in February 2009, the bridge was inspected and reopened the same day, showcasing its resilience and the rapid response of Indiana and Kentucky transportation officials."
